        "Rafi Bistritzer",
        "Allan H. MacDonald",
        "Pablo Jarillo-Herrero"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Moiré flat bands and the resulting correlated phases opened a powerful new route to create and study quantum states in tunable materials.",
        "attribution": "Bistritzer and MacDonald predicted the magic-angle mechanism; Jarillo-Herrero led the experiments that established correlated insulating and superconducting states.",
        "maturity": "The central observations have been reproduced in multiple devices and materials, and the field has developed rapidly since the initial discovery.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The microscopic origin of superconductivity and the extent to which distinct moiré systems share a common mechanism remain unsettled."
        ]
      }
    },
