      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattices made controlled quantum simulation of many-body phenomena possible, including direct access to regimes difficult to study in solid materials.",
        "attribution": "Bloch and Greiner established important experimental capabilities and results; Cirac helped develop the theoretical framework for quantum simulation with ultracold atoms.",
        "maturity": "The platform is mature and has produced a substantial body of reproducible results, though its role as a general simulator continues to evolve.",
